Final Truth (No confusion, no tricks)

For a Top-5 table visual, you MUST apply
“Measure → is not blank” as a visual filter.

There is no pure-DAX solution that:

Shows only Top 5 rows

Shows correct per-row values

Shows correct Grand Total
without either:

a visual filter, or

a separate Top-5 dimension table

This is by design in Power BI.

🧠 Why this is unavoidable (important concept)
Power BI evaluation order:

Visual rows are decided first (ProductID list)

Measures are evaluated later

Measures cannot delete rows

They can only return values or BLANK

So:

To remove rows → visual filter

To fix totals → SUMX

To control row vs total logic → ISINSCOPE

